Iomenei is the largest of the striders of [[Geography/Istria/index|Istria]]: a man-made hulk of a mountain that walks on six legs and carries a city of 100,000 people. It was built almost immediately after the gods first came to [[Færrin]], and it is one of the oldest structures still operating there.

The city walks through Istria, keeping clear of curses, ancient beasts and the weapons of war left by wizards from before the Fracture. It crosses the Deadlands and moves along the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|Infinite Horizon]] by slipping from world to world, stopping only to pick up ancient treasures and archaeotech from the Dark Ages, things that can no longer be made or that are forbidden to study. The jumps are dangerous: a bad one loses pieces of the city or warps them where they lie, and the mutants of the [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/Undercroft|Undercroft]] are blamed on one that went badly wrong. The strider's predominant religion is the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Eternal Pulse|Pulse]], the faith of a machine that lives forever by spending people as its fuel.

Iomenei is a symbiotic mass. Its heroes live on the upper decks, literally upper, and are showered with gifts for delving into the ancient places and clearing them of what lives inside. They do not operate the city. The engines, the fuel, the cargo and every other task fall to the tens of thousands of crofters below, in the Undercroft. The Seneschal is the city's second-in-command.

Of late Iomenei has had trouble. Fires have started, clan leaders of the Undercroft have been killed in ways that each looked natural but that together form a pattern, and two of the strider's six legs froze for six seconds. That was not long enough for the [[Phenomena/Stillness|Stillness]] to catch up, but it was enough for the Seneschal to fear foul play. Rather than endanger the heroes above decks, he put out a command among the Undercrofters: find whoever is sabotaging the city and bring them to justice, and earn a place on the upper decks.

The sabotage was found in Strider Leg Armature Containment Unit 14, one of the openings near the bottom of the strider where a leg enters the body so that its joints can be repaired and fresh lubricant fed in through intake pipes. The room is a domed space about 300 feet across, dominated by the 200 feet of leg inside it, with rigging around the leg and about 85 workers in the sector. Someone had wedged a piece of scrap metal into one of the leg's lubricant lines, so that the lubricant would slowly run out and the leg would seize.

The foreman of the sector had the scrap removed and thrown away before anyone could study it. He knew what it meant for him: a foreman who lets such a thing happen on his watch is a dead man walking, and only the fact that no one had gotten around to executing him yet had kept him alive. When [[People/Barlow Crane|Barlow Crane]] told him as much and told him to run, he fled out through the opening where the leg enters.

Barlow Crane read the emotions left on the lubricant line and saw the face of whoever had handled it: an elf, perhaps a man, with a jaw split into mandibles and small closed eyelids dotted around his eyes, and an overwhelming sense of religious devotion. The face matched [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], and the mark of a horn inside a circle, Herald's symbol, was later found scratched into the bedpost of the elven fluid master [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]]. Gerhard is the saboteur, and he was not found.
